# Authors, order and affiliations as in the napari-TurboBox Application Note.
# ORCID iDs are given where the manuscript lists one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use napari-TurboBox, please cite it using the metadata from this
  file.
type: software
title: napari-TurboBox
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/N-Friederich/napari-turbobox"
url: "https://github.com/N-Friederich/napari-turbobox"
abstract: >-
  Promptable segmentation models segment 3D target objects from a single
  axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) into a full 3D instance mask, which makes
  fast, accurate box placement the rate-limiting step when annotating large
  volumetric images. Placing a box well is a multi-viewer task, editing in one
  slice and checking against the orthogonal views. napari-TurboBox is a napari
  plugin that keeps all boxes in one shared store for all viewers: one viewer
  is used for editing, the others show the same boxes read-only. Boxes stay
  axis-aligned while they are moved or resized and can be exported as
  per-slice COCO and YOLO annotations.
keywords:
  - napari
  - bounding box annotation
  - volumetric microscopy
  - promptable segmentation
  - multi-viewer synchronization
  - COCO
  - YOLO
